{"causes": ["The early persecution of Muslims in Mecca led Hatib to migrate to Medina, joining the nascent Muslim community.", "His participation in the Battle of Badr in 624 CE established his high standing among the Companions of Prophet Muhammad.", "The ongoing conflict between the early Muslim community and the Quraysh of Mecca created the context for his diplomatic and military roles."], "effects": ["Hatib's diplomatic mission to Egypt in 628 CE initiated an important early contact between the emerging Islamic state and Byzantium's Egyptian province.", "His controversial letter before the Conquest of Mecca led to a direct Qur'anic revelation, shaping early Islamic legal and ethical thought on loyalty.", "His forgiveness by Prophet Muhammad set a precedent for mercy and the high regard for veterans of the Battle of Badr in Islamic tradition."], "relationships": [{"sourceSlug": "muhammad", "sourceName": "Muhammad", "verb": "COLLABORATES_WITH", "targetSlug": "hatib-ibn-abi-baltaah", "targetName": "Hatib ibn Abi Balta'ah", "context": "Hatib ibn Abi Balta'ah served as an envoy and military companion to Prophet Muhammad throughout his prophetic mission."}, {"sourceSlug": "hatib-ibn-abi-baltaah", "sourceName": "Hatib ibn Abi Balta'ah", "verb": "PARTICIPATES_IN", "targetSlug": "battle-of-badr", "targetName": "Battle of Badr", "context": "Hatib ibn Abi Balta'ah was a veteran of the Battle of Badr in 624 CE, a foundational victory for the early Muslim community."}, {"sourceSlug": "hatib-ibn-abi-baltaah", "sourceName": "Hatib ibn Abi Balta'ah", "verb": "OCCURS_IN", "targetSlug": "medina", "targetName": "Medina, Arabian Peninsula", "context": "Hatib ibn Abi Balta'ah resided in Medina after the Hijra, serving the Prophet Muhammad and the early Muslim community from this city."}, {"sourceSlug": "conquest-of-mecca", "sourceName": "Conquest of Mecca", "verb": "FRAMES", "targetSlug": "hatib-ibn-abi-baltaah", "targetName": "Hatib ibn Abi Balta'ah", "context": "The events leading